  "details": "Alternative/supplementary idea to configuring avatar performance ranks locally to your own needs https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/settings-or-config-file-for-avatar-performance-limitsrating \n\nBut instead of customising each performance rank, we could customise one set of settings defining how big total budget we have for all avatars in the instance. \n\nLike I'm willing to display for example 1M polys, 15GB of vram, 200 materials, 4 lights, 4 cloths  \n\nThen each avatar that is loaded would slowly use up that budget until it's full and then biggest/most far away (should be setting?) avatar should be hidden or have given components disabled - just how performance limiter works today, so i could still see cloth of 4 people closest to me and the rest would be just static mesh, but I don't need to see that 2M poly avatar of someone crazy\n\nI think this should allow us to control how much we can handle much more precisely, while avatar performance limits don't really reflect much - as I might be able to handle 20 poor avatars, but probably not when they all enable single light. This setting would scale well between small and big instances, automatically allowing only more optimised avatars when there is more people around you - or focusing on showing people closest to you (This should be a setting)",
